            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A system for delivering a fastener may comprise a fastener delivery tool. The fastener delivery tool may comprise a sheath assembly having at least one position retention member proximate a distal end of the sheath assembly, and a handle assembly coupled to a proximal end of the sheath assembly, the handle assembly comprising a housing, a trigger handle, and an insert connector, and an insert including a proximal head, shaft, and distal end. When the insert is received within the sheath assembly, the shaft may be disposed within a lumen of the sheath assembly while the proximal head may be disposed proximate the insert connector. An external force applied to the trigger handle may be transferred to the insert connector to cause the insert connector to translate in a proximal direction, thereby applying force in the proximal direction to the proximal head of the insert to cause the received insert to move in the proximal direction.</p>
            </abstract>
